  "scope": "# Review \u2014 7b088f161470\n\nTask/source: assigned generator `7b088f161470`; approved baseline `4.0.0` \u2192 proposed repaired `4.1.0`; current source SHA-256 `ee796bd6fc60f5b0bb9664351830177d22c4b00a8fcdcc15164ba93ce1100a45`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: generalized lessons made row-presence proportional to full rungs, so `floor(colored_rows/2)` fit every lesson; incomplete side-only distractor rows now break that rival on all eight declared profiles without changing true labels, and optional blank padding is capped so every generated grid stays within ARC\u2019s 30\u00d730 limit.\nCanonical authority: unchanged Racket source (raw SHA-256 `5cb73bc4092b61cc885c0ad3c2ec1cf301bb02c288dcd3462aa4d85c370c4bfc`; normalized hash `5cb6f6518f37c8a2c4e690273e7ca0fe86c72c8eff864d51874132a9f615f6d5`), unchanged canonical profiles, and no shared-data edit.\nParametric deliverable: separate task-local prototype with episode-fixed rung threshold `3|4|5` and bar alignment `left|right`; default `(3,left)` is byte-exact canonical Racket.\nPrototype contract: three labeled demonstrations, four distinct unlabeled queries, exact public-byte IDs, private settings/query answers, duplicate rejection, and demonstration-only separation of all six declared settings.\nFocused verification: final selected-task suite reports 25 passing tests; the retained all-settings run executed six Racket programs and 24 query labels, with canonical parity `8/8` over four unique canonical inputs.\nTeaching evidence: all eight generalized profiles have Racket/mirror agreement and defeat the row-count rival; see `checks/shortcut-repair-7b088f161470-v2/report.json`.\nSupplementary tickets: API boundary `017f1406edaf` completed cleanly; adversarial witness `628b4a2c24c1` reproduced a source-bound wall-required shortcut and is reported in `AUDIT.md`.\nRemaining limit: the parameter family is proposed only\u2014no production parameter API, catalog approval, or training admission\u2014and identifiability is bounded to the declared six-setting family.\nDisposition: main repair and bounded prototype are complete; maintainer attention is needed only for prototype promotion policy and the independent peer finding.",
